{% set local_problem %}
<p>Many Hazel Green properties have significant tree coverage — it's part of what makes the area attractive. But those trees are constantly dropping debris into your gutters. Pine needles year-round. Oak and maple leaves in fall. Twigs and seeds throughout the year.</p>

<p>Without protection, Hazel Green homeowners find themselves cleaning gutters 3-4 times annually or paying $150-200+ per cleaning. That adds up fast. And when gutters clog between cleanings, water overflows and heads for your foundation.</p>

<p>Gutter guards solve this problem permanently. They keep debris out while letting rainwater through. The result is gutters that flow freely year-round with minimal maintenance.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers or screens that fit over or inside your gutters, blocking debris while allowing water to enter. Different types work better for different debris challenges.</p>

<p>Micro-mesh guards excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles. Screen guards handle larger leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water in while debris slides off. We'll assess your specific situation and recommend the best solution during your free estimate.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed gutter guards on properties throughout Hazel Green and understand the area's debris challenges. We'll recommend the right solution for your trees and situation — not just sell you whatever's most expensive.</p>

